            <ArticleTitle>More Is Less: IL-9 in the Resolution of Inflammation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>403-405</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1074-7613(17)30386-2</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.immuni.2017.09.004</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a recent study in Nature Medicine, Rauber et al. (2017) identify interleukin-9 (IL-9) derived from group 2 innate lymphoid cells as crucial regulators inducing resolution of chronic inflammation in rheumatoid arthritis. Their findings provide insight into the varied functions of IL-9 and open the door to novel therapeutic interventions.</AbstractText>
